<section class="legal-page">
    <div class="container container-narrow">
        <partial name="_LegalNav" model='(string)"DMCA"' />

        <div class="legal-header">
            <h1 class="legal-title">DMCA Notice &amp; Copyright Takedown Procedure</h1>
            <div class="legal-meta">
                <span>17 U.S.C. § 512 &bull; Digital Millennium Copyright Act Compliance</span>
                <span>Last Updated: October 19, 2026</span>
                <span>Safe Harbor &bull; Designated Compliance Agent</span>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="legal-content">
            <div class="highlight-box">
                <strong>IMPORTANT NOTICE FOR RIGHTS HOLDERS:</strong> SaveZonix is an open software utility and client-side stream inspector. <strong>We do NOT host, store, mirror, cache, stream, or re-transmit any video, audio, or media files on our servers.</strong> All media transfers take place directly and strictly between the user's personal device and the third-party web server hosting the file. However, in compliance with 17 U.S.C. § 512 and international copyright conventions, we maintain an expeditious takedown procedure to remove or disable any infringing documentation, links, or technical presets under our direct control.
            </div>

            <h2>1. Designated Copyright &amp; DMCA Agent</h2>
            <p>Pursuant to 17 U.S.C. § 512(c), all notifications of claimed copyright infringement concerning our website, software repositories, or documentation should be submitted to our Designated Compliance Agent:</p>
            <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.7); border: 1px solid var(--border-color); border-radius: var(--radius-md); padding: 22px; margin: 18px 0;">
                <p style="margin: 0 0 6px 0; font-size: 15px; color: #fff;"><strong>SaveZonix Legal &amp; Compliance Department</strong></p>
                <p style="margin: 0 0 6px 0;">Designated DMCA Agent: Compliance &amp; IP Protection Desk</p>
                <p style="margin: 0 0 6px 0;">Official Email: <a href="mailto:savezonix@gmail.com" class="auth-link">savezonix@gmail.com</a></p>
                <p style="margin: 0 0 6px 0;">Response Time: Within 24–48 business hours</p>
                <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 12px; color: var(--text-muted);">Please use the subject line: <em>"DMCA Copyright Infringement Notification — [Name of Rights Holder]"</em></p>
            </div>

            <h2>2. Elements of a Legally Valid DMCA Notice</h2>
            <p>Under 17 U.S.C. § 512(c)(3), an effective copyright infringement notification must be provided in writing to our designated agent and must include the following information:</p>
            <ol>
                <li><strong>Physical or Electronic Signature:</strong> A physical or electronic signature of a person authorized to act on behalf of the owner of an exclusive right that is allegedly infringed.</li>
                <li><strong>Identification of Copyrighted Work:</strong> Identification of the copyrighted work claimed to have been infringed, or if multiple works are covered by a single notification, a representative list of such works.</li>
                <li><strong>Identification of Infringing Material:</strong> Identification of the specific webpage URL, documentation link, technical reference, or code repository claimed to be infringing, with sufficient information to allow us to locate the material.</li>
                <li><strong>Contact Information:</strong> Information reasonably sufficient to permit us to contact the complaining party, including legal name, physical address, telephone number, and official corporate email address.</li>
                <li><strong>Good-Faith Statement:</strong> A statement that the complaining party has a good-faith belief that use of the material in the manner complained of is not authorized by the copyright owner, its agent, or the law.</li>
                <li><strong>Perjury Statement:</strong> A statement that the information in the notification is accurate, and under penalty of perjury, that the complaining party is authorized to act on behalf of the owner of an exclusive right that is allegedly infringed.</li>
            </ol>
            <p style="font-size: 12.5px; color: #f87171;"><em>Note: Under 17 U.S.C. § 512(f), any person who knowingly materially misrepresents that material is infringing may be subject to statutory liability and damages, including costs and attorney's fees.</em></p>

            <h2>3. Counter-Notification Procedures</h2>
            <p>If you believe that your content, link, or reference was removed or disabled as a result of mistake or misidentification, you may submit a written counter-notification pursuant to 17 U.S.C. § 512(g)(2) and (3). The counter-notification must contain:</p>
            <ul>
                <li>Your physical or electronic signature;</li>
                <li>Identification of the material that has been removed or to which access has been disabled, and the location at which the material appeared before removal;</li>
                <li>A statement under penalty of perjury that you have a good-faith belief that the material was removed or disabled as a result of mistake or misidentification;</li>
                <li>Your name, address, telephone number, and a statement consenting to the jurisdiction of the federal district court for your judicial district.</li>
            </ul>

            <h2>4. Repeat Infringer Policy (17 U.S.C. § 512(i))</h2>
            <p>SaveZonix maintains a strict repeat infringer policy. We will terminate, disable, or revoke accounts, API access, or service permissions of users who are repeatedly determined to have infringed third-party copyrights or violated our Acceptable Use Policy.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
